stribution is a containerized Python service (needs container). PG has pgserver... The investigation doesn't really need to run components — it's desk analysis + planning decision. Score 0 (can't meaningfully exercise the provisioning paths without a cluster). I'll say 0 with rationale.\n\nE002 ai_signals: cs=1, pp=1, ap=0, ef=1, oq=1, ed=1, hpg=0, ra=1, ac=1.\nE003: cs=1, pp=0, ap=0, ef=0, oq=1, ed=1, hpg=0, ra=1, ac=1.\nBranch A: cs=1, pp=1, ap=1, ef=1, oq=-1, ed=-1, hpg=0, ra=1, ac=1.\nBranch B: cs=1, pp=1, ap=1, ef=1, oq=-1, ed=1, hpg=0, ra=1, ac=1.\nBranch C: cs=1, pp=1, ap=0, ef=1, oq=1, ed=1, hpg=0, ra=1, ac=1.\n\nNow write the files. Use Write tool for bodies (no frontmatter delimiters), then frontmatter.py set.\n\nWait — \"Write the body content (no frontmatter delimiters)\" then `frontmatter.py set` — the script presumably prepends frontmatter. Let me verify write_frontmatter handles a file with no frontmatter. It should. Let me just do it and validate with `read`.\n\nAlso state.py — should I persist state? The prompt for decompose-agent doesn't mandate state persistence; CLAUDE.md says long-running skills use state.py. Not strictly needed; skip to keep it lean. Actually, let me not bother.\n\nDirectory: artifacts/epic-tasks/ — check it exists.","signature":"4607bb395b52497fadecf33935cbb064"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76348,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8ad4966f4dc767f","agent_id":"acde594ef08b59665","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"3f86328a-cafc-4c62-b6c8-ee4f6bc09b0a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:48:15.557Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
