{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6cb3282143a02c1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based self-provisioning of the default pgvector instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not deliver a RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time, re-implement provisioning\n18\t    as BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own PostgreSQL per the go/no-go decision's\n19\t    other outcomes.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-based self-provisioning of the default pgvector instance\n37\t\n38\t> Conditional branch A — instantiated only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects operator-based self-provisioning (the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164, delivers a RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the target release).\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tThis epic implements out-of-the-box provisioning of the default vector store using the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164). Self-provisioning PostgreSQL for Gen AI Studio following the model-registry-operator pattern requires a RHOAI-controlled operator; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic. When a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG is configured, the operator provisions a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector (using the existing Red Hat `postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector out of the box) and wires the OGX instance to use it as its vector I/O provider.\n43\t\n44\tThe implementation must remain portable to the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL planned for RHOAI 3.6: the consuming configuration is a connection string, so the shared database can replace self-provisioning without redesign.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization: provisioning the database Deployment, Service, persistent storage, and credentials Secret per namespace, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern as the reference implementation.\n49\t- Wire the provisioned instance into the OGX server configuration for playgrounds with RAG, activating the remote pgvector vector I/O provider with the provisioned connection details.\n50\t- Scope instances per namespace for multi-tenant isolation (per-namespace is the resolved scoping direction; the per-instance consumer, Auto Rag, is handled in RHAISTRAT-7824).\n51\t- Apply resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing, adjusted per the benchmark recommendation where available.\n52\t- Design for portability: the OGX configuration consumes a connection string, so a platform-provided shared database (RHOAI 3.6) can replace self-provisioning without changes to the consuming side.\n53\t- Handle lifecycle end-to-end in the operator: creation, upgrade, credential management, and cleanup when the owning playground (or its namespace resources) is deleted.\n54\t\n55\tOut of scope: the OGX-side provider enablement (delivered by the distribution's remote pgvector provider configuration); benchmarking; Auto Rag compatibility (RHAISTRAT-7824); the platform-shared database itself (RHOAI 3.6).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A user who creates a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG capabilities gets a working default vector store with no manual provisioning or external infrastructure configuration (out-of-the-box experience preserved).\n60\t- The PostgreSQL/pgvector instance (Deployment, Service, persistent storage, credentials Secret) is provisioned and managed by the operator, and is cleaned up when the owning playground is deleted.\n61\t- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function end-to-end against the default vector store with no loss of current capability (document ingestion, retrieval, and query flows).\n62\t- Vector store instances are isolated per namespace; one namespace's playground cannot read another namespace's vector data through the default store.\n63\t- The provisioned instance's resource requests/limits follow the agreed sizing (model-registry-operator reference, adjusted per benchmark where applicable) and run without significant overhead in resource-constrained environments.\n64\t- The OGX-side wiring consumes a connection-string style configuration, so a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL can replace the self-provisioned instance without changes to the consuming configuration.\n65\t- The pgvector-capable PostgreSQL image reference used for provisioning is resolvable in disconnected installs (the related image env var already present in the rhods-operator CSV).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning: delivered by operator-based self-provisioning.\n70\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability: end-to-end validation acceptance criteria above.\n71\t- **HLR-4 (P1, bundled)** — multi-tenant scoping (per-namespace isolation): a property of the same provisioning surface; bundled rather than split.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84927dd4c0085fae","agent_id":"af44f3bd2f5ac49aa","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"7384997f-e8ad-47f6-b8cb-0634246baba7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:53:18.510Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6cb3282143a02c1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
