r to confirm. |\n14\t| human_judgment_required | -2 | The gating question is itself a human planning decision: the Staff Engineer Input explicitly directs that the go/no-go gate be defined and run as part of sprint planning, and it hinges on another strategy's delivery timing and a release commitment. The AI can prepare the analysis and criteria, but the selection is a governance/scheduling decision it cannot make. |\n15\t\n16\tRouting implication: Low — assign to a person (the Gen AI Studio team running\n17\tsprint planning), with the desk-research portions (lifecycle and portability\n18\tanalysis of each option) prepared as input.\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84927dd4c0085fae","agent_id":"af44f3bd2f5ac49aa","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"807c9810-8135-4119-b87c-e44e63a95311","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:53:23.547Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a34fbe07e510a67e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
