body references sibling epics by\ndraft ID (verified by scan — only structured frontmatter fields contain epic\nIDs).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy acceptance criteria are accounted for: out-of-the-box default\n(branches A/B; branch C records the staff-directed deferral explicitly),\nplayground RAG function (E002 + branch ACs), separate process (E002),\nmulti-tenant scoping (branches, HLR-4), lightweight/resource-constrained\n(E003 sizing + branch ACs), and Auto Rag descoped with a visible record\n(HLR-7) rather than silent drop. Every Staff Engineer Input item is carried\nforward: no image build/onboarding (Correction 2), portability to the 3.6\nshared database (E001 analysis + branch scope/ACs), RHAISTRAT-7164 hard\ndependency and go/no-go gate in sprint planning (E001), BFF fallback with its\ncaveats (branch B), BYO fallback aligned with OGX 1.0 breaking changes\n(branch C), disconnected-install image resolution (branch ACs), and\nmodel-registry-operator sizing reference (E003 + branches). Both strategy open\nquestions are explicitly dispositioned (per-namespace scoping resolved;\nmigration path resolved to an AC). The conditional branches cover all three\nbounded outcomes named in the Staff Engineer Input. The missing strategy\nattachment (Affected Components, Impacted Teams, formal HLRs, NFRs) is\nsurfaced as a Health Warning with team assignments inferred and flagged for\nverification — the correct handling of an input gap, not a silent drop. No\ndocs-authoring epic is required: the visible strategy declares no\nDocumentation Support gate.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48488,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84927dd4c0085fae","agent_id":"af44f3bd2f5ac49aa","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"88dabf0d-6aed-4ca9-b9e3-1b0b1d282b2e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:58:26.605Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","tas