d forces that criterion to 0.\n38\t\n39\t## Criterion Details\n40\t\n41\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n42\tAll P0 HLRs (HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3) map to epics; P1 HLRs (HLR-4, HLR-5) are covered;\n43\tP2 HLR-6 is bundled into E002 with a recorded bundled rationale in both the matrix row\n44\tand the epic's HLR Traceability section. HLR-7 (Auto Rag criterion) is descoped per\n45\tStaff Engineer override 5 and visibly recorded in the matrix rather than silently\n46\tdropped — a justified descope, not a gap. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 (P0)\n47\tgates the P0 branch epics, E002 (P0) blocks the P0 branch epics, and the P1 benchmark\n48\tepic E003 blocks no P0 work. Priority collapse checks pass: HLR-4 (per-namespace\n49\tisolation, P1) bundled into the P0 branch epics is an incidental property of the same\n50\tprovisioning surface, not a deferrable independent feature, and is flagged as bundled;\n51\tHLR-6 (P2) is documentation of the same config surface E002 implements, also flagged.\n52\t\n53\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n54\tNo circular dependencies. Diagram (arrows dependency → dependent) matches frontmatter\n55\texactly: E003 depends on E002; each branch epic depends on E001 and E002; E001 and E002\n56\thave no dependencies. All three branch files set both `branch` (A/B/C, matching\n57\tfilenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`, and no main-plan epic lists a branch\n58\tepic in its dependencies. Edges verified against the construction rules: E002 → branch\n59\tepics is a genuine Rule 13 artifact dependency (the branches wire OGX instances against\n60\tthe remote pgvector provider surface E002 delivers in the distribution build — E002 is\n61\ta general implementation epic, not a build-pipeline output consumed as content, so the\n62\tAC-gate-only coupling restriction does not apply). E001 ∥ E002 and E003 ∥ branches are\n63\tcorrectly parallel; the E003 ∥ branches decision is explicitly documented in the DAG\n64\tjustification, and the branch epics treat benchmark sizing as \"adjusted per benchmark\n65\twhere available\" with a defined starting point (model-registry-operator sizing), so\n66\tthere is no undiscovered hard data dependency. Critical path length 2 is reasonable for\n67\tthis strategy size.\n68\t\n69\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (0/2)\n70\tComponent/team tuples are clean (E002 = OGX Core/OGX; all provisioning-side epics =\n71\tGen AI Studio/Gen AI Studio). The branch B size overage is handled correctly: kept as\n72\tone logical change WITH a concrete recorded re-split trigger (split out lifecycle work\n73\tif it needs reconciliation machinery) — a managed trade-off, not a violation. Branch\n74\tepics are mutually exclusive alternatives, not scope duplication. However,\n75\t**BRANCH-C-E004 bundles code implementation with content authoring**: its scope\n76\tincludes both implementation work (OGXServer config support, playground indication\n77\tsurface) and a substantive user-facing setup guide (\"Document the setup end to end\",\n78\tvalidated by a clean-environment walk-through AC). The decomposition's own Health\n79\tWarning concedes \"the documentation is a primary work product, not incidental polish\",\n80\tyet keeps the bundle with only a \"re-examine later\" watch note. Unlike the branch B\n81\tsize overage, there is no recorded-trigger mechanism that sanctions carrying a\n82\twork-product mix forward — the rule is that code implementation and content authoring\n83\tare different kinds of work with different review criteria and must be separate epics\n84\teven when owned by the same team. This is a major issue; Criterion 3 scores 0.\n85\t\n86\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n87\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (which of three bounded provisioning\n88\tmechanisms exists) determines which branch epic is instantiated — it changes downstream\n89\tstructure, not just scheduling. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts\n90\t(provider configuration, benchmark report, provisioning mechanisms). Every gated epic\n91\tsets `gated_by` to an epic in its direct `dependencies` list, and every\n92\t`gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and a populated `fallback_approach`. No epic\n93\tlists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by`.\n94\t\n95\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n96\tType-appropriate signal fields are used throughout: E001 carries `investigation_signals`\n97\t(5-signal rubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all Implementation epics carry `ai_signals`\n98\twith `investigation_signals: null`. Signal values are consistent with the strategy\n99\tcontent and the cited `.context` files: E001's `source_accessibility: 0` /\n100\t`human_judgment_required: -2` correctly reflect that the go/no-go hinges on\n101\tRHAISTRAT-7164 delivery timing and a sprint-planning governance decision; branch A's\n102\t`open_questions: -1` / `external_dependency: -1` correctly reflect the hard\n103\tRHAISTRAT-7164 dependency, while branch B (which exists precisely when that dependency\n104\tdoes not land) scores `external_dependency: +1`. `architecture_claims: +1` rationales\n105\tcite the actual architecture-context files (ogx-distribution.md, model-registry-\n106\toperator.md, ogx-k8s-operator.md, odh-dashboard.md, ai4rag.md — all present in\n107\t`.context`), so the calibration is grounded, not merely internally consistent.\n108\t\n109\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n110\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy and Staff Engineer\n111\tinput. No rule-mandated AC is missing: there are no replacement epics (rollback/flag),\n112\tno konflux chain (Staff Engineer Correction 2 eliminated it — E002 instead carries an\n113\tenv-guard-defaults AC), and no docs-authoring epic (see Criterion 7). No AC states an\n114\texternally-controlled precondition — the branch epics' disconnected-install ACs are\n115\tconditions on the epics' own configuration deliverables, and the sizing ACs reference a\n116\tdefined starting point. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n117\t\n118\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n119\tAll strategy acceptance criteria are accounted for: out-of-the-box (branch epics),\n120\tplayground RAG function (E002 + branch epics), separate-process store (E002),\n121\tmulti-tenant scoping (HLR-4 in branches), lightweight/resource footprint (E003), and\n122\tthe Auto Rag criterion visibly descoped per explicit Staff Engineer direction with the\n123\tredirect to RHAISTRAT-7824 recorded. Both strategy open questions are dispositioned\n124\t(scoping model resolved to per-namespace; migration path became an E002 AC), and the\n125\tremoved latency/corpus/index open questions follow Staff Engineer override 6. Strategy\n126\trisks and context are carried forward: the RHAISTRAT-7164 hard dependency is modeled as\n127\tthe gating structure plus Health Warnings, the BFF fallback is branch B, and the\n128\tmissing strategy attachment is flagged as a Health Warning rather than silently\n129\tignored. The strategy declares no Documentation Support requirement, so no docs-authoring\n130\tepic is mandated by Rule 11 (validator confirms docs-last coverage is not applicable).\n131\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91d83d54e068c69a","agent_id":"af523506aa080761a","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"4c7512d1-56d1-4327-adb4-56cb5544dd8d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:04:48.306Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a618adcf82739529","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
