{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-877d254d-43f0-48f3-ba31-2e639efe37d9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9176405d426b1cb1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-_gv0xqa4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E005.md","content":"# Document the bring-your-own PostgreSQL setup for playground RAG\n\n> Conditional branch C — instantiated only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects bring-your-own PostgreSQL (neither operator-based nor BFF-managed provisioning is viable for the target release). Docs-authoring epic: runs docs-last, blocked by the bring-your-own configuration-support implementation it documents.\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors the end-to-end user-facing setup documentation for the bring-your-own PostgreSQL fallback: the procedure by which a user or administrator attaches a user-supplied PostgreSQL (with pgvector) to an OGX instance so that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows run against it. The documentation is a primary work product of this outcome, not incidental polish — the Staff Engineer Input notes that the playground largely abstracts OGX from users, so the written procedure is where the configuration burden lands. It is a separate docs-authoring epic because code implementation and content authoring are different kinds of work with different review criteria, and it is scheduled docs-last: the guide is finalized and technically reviewed only after the configuration support it describes has landed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Author the end-to-end setup guide: preparing a PostgreSQL+pgvector instance, creating the credentials Secret, configuring the OGXServer spec with the PostgreSQL connection details, and verifying RAG works.\n- Cover the disconnected-install path, where the user's PostgreSQL must be reachable from the cluster.\n- Document the credentials Secret handling and the connection-details format, consistent with the secret-reference (never inline) convention the configuration support enforces.\n- Cross-link the playground's no-vector-store indication to the documented configuration path so the guidance is discoverable from the UI.\n\nOut of scope: the configuration support itself (OGXServer spec fields, credentials Secret wiring, playground indication — delivered by the bring-your-own implementation epic of this branch); the OGX-side remote pgvector provider enablement; benchmarking and resource sizing; Auto Rag compatibility (RHAISTRAT-7824).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The documented setup procedure is complete and has been validated on a clean environment, including the credentials Secret handling and connection details format, and including the disconnected-install path.\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation as built (the configuration support actually delivered, not as planned), and the review is recorded.\n- The documented configuration path remains the migration target for users outgrowing any future default store (consistent with the migration path off the default vector database).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0, fallback form)** — in this branch the out-of-the-box default is explicitly not delivered; the documented setup procedure is the user-facing deliverable through which the bring-your-own requirement is met to the extent the Staff Engineer Input directs for this outcome.\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — the clean-environment walk-through of the documented procedure is the end-to-end validation that playground RAG workflows function with the user-provided vector store with no loss of current capability.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44617,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91d83d54e068c69a","agent_id":"af523506aa080761a","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"38f59882-d