{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-816d50e5e46d17f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set default resource\n4\t  sizing\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set default resource sizing\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic validates the pgvector choice empirically and produces the resource sizing for the default vector store instance. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the default pgvector instance is meant for development experimentation, not production usage: there are no strict latency SLAs (no p50/p95/p99 thresholds), and the benchmark's pass condition is that pgvector performs in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline on typical playground RAG document sets — small document collections where a flat scan (no vector index) is expected to be sufficient. Users with production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database.\n36\t\n37\tThe sizing deliverable starts from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits as the reference point, adjusted if the benchmark results warrant.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline: vector insert and retrieval timings for representative playground RAG workloads (small document sets ingested and queried through the playground's RAG flow).\n42\t- Run the same workloads against a development-provisioned PostgreSQL+pgvector instance using the OGX distribution's remote pgvector provider.\n43\t- Compare results and record whether pgvector is within the same order of magnitude as the baseline (order-of-magnitude comparison, not a fixed threshold).\n44\t- Confirm (or refute) that flat scan (no vector index) is sufficient for typical playground document sets, and record the corpus-size boundary if one is observed.\n45\t- Produce the resource sizing recommendation (requests/limits) for the default pgvector instance, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing, adjusted based on the measured results.\n46\t\n47\tOut of scope: latency SLA definitions; index type selection beyond the flat-scan confirmation; production-scale corpus testing; provisioning mechanism work.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A benchmark report exists that captures the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector measurements for representative playground RAG workloads, using the distribution build with the remote pgvector provider enabled.\n52\t- The report states, with data, whether pgvector is within the same order of magnitude of the inline Milvus baseline (order-of-magnitude comparison; no fixed latency threshold is applied).\n53\t- The report confirms flat scan (no index) is sufficient for typical playground document sets, or documents the observed boundary where it is not.\n54\t- A resource sizing recommendation (requests/limits) for the default pgvector instance is produced, referencing the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing as its starting point and noting any benchmark-driven adjustment.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-5 (P1)** — the default vector store is lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments without significant overhead: this epic's sizing deliverable is the measured basis for that requirement; the selected provisioning epic applies the recommendation as its resource configuration.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfd2a0f76a0d748","agent_id":"ac4f00ce08696bdb4","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"cffa2dc3-429a-4010-a1b9-23fe4c1d2e47","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:10:17.065Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-816d50e5e46d17f0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final re-review of RHAISTRAT-8004"}
