{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-954071b2bc0067ce","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E004\n3\ttitle: Bring-your-own PostgreSQL support for playground RAG\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If a self-provisioning mechanism (operator-based or BFF-managed)\n17\t    becomes viable for the release after all, rewrite this branch to the selected\n18\t    self-provisioning approach to restore the out-of-the-box experience.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 7\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Bring-your-own PostgreSQL support for playground RAG\n36\t\n37\t> Conditional branch C — instantiated only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects bring-your-own PostgreSQL (neither operator-based nor BFF-managed provisioning is viable for the target release).\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic implements the deliberate fallback in which customers provide their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the Gen AI Studio playground: users (or administrators) configure the OGXServer custom resource spec with their PostgreSQL connection details, and the playground's RAG workflows run against that database using the remote pgvector vector I/O provider. The Staff Engineer Input notes this aligns with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0, even though the playground largely abstracts OGX from users — so this epic also carries the burden of making the configuration path as discoverable and low-friction as the playground permits. The end-to-end user-facing setup documentation for this configuration path is a primary work product and is delivered by a separate docs-authoring epic in this branch, scheduled docs-last after this implementation so it is technically reviewed against the configuration support as built.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Support and validate the configuration path by which a user-supplied PostgreSQL (with pgvector) is attached to an OGX instance for playground RAG: OGXServer custom resource spec fields and the credentials Secret carrying connection details.\n46\t- Surface the bring-your-own requirement in the Gen AI Studio playground where the abstraction would otherwise hide it: clear indication when no default vector store is available and RAG is requested, with guidance to the configuration path.\n47\t- Validate that the configuration path works end to end with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider enabled in the OGX distribution (document ingestion, retrieval, and query flows against a user-supplied database).\n48\t- Confirm per-namespace behavior: user-supplied instances and their credentials are referenced and scoped within the owning namespace.\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: the OGX-side provider enablement (delivered by the distribution's remote pgvector provider configuration); provisioning a default instance (this branch exists precisely when that is not viable); benchmarking; Auto Rag compatibility (RHAISTRAT-7824); the end-to-end user-facing setup documentation and its clean-environment walk-through (delivered by the docs-authoring epic of this branch).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A user-supplied PostgreSQL with pgvector, configured via the OGXServer spec and a credentials Secret, serves vector I/O for playground RAG workflows, verified end to end (document ingestion, retrieval, and query flows).\n55\t- The playground clearly indicates when RAG is unavailable because no vector store is configured, and points to the documented configuration path.\n56\t- Credentials are supplied via Secret references, never inline in the custom resource spec or exposed in process arguments.\n57\t- User-supplied instances and credentials remain scoped to the owning namespace (no cross-namespace leakage through the playground path).\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- **HLR-1 (P0, fallback form)** — in this branch the out-of-the-box default is explicitly not delivered; the requirement is satisfied to the extent the Staff Engineer Input directs for this outcome (bring-your-own aligned with the OGX 1.0 breaking changes), and the strategy-level out-of-the-box criterion is recorded as consciously deferred. The user-facing setup documentation through which customers exercise this path is carried by the docs-authoring epic of this branch.\n62\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — playground RAG workflows function with the user-provided vector store with no loss of current capability; engineering verification lives here, and the clean-environment walk-through of the documented procedure is the docs-authoring epic's acceptance criterion.\n63\t- **HLR-4 (P1, bundled)** — multi-tenant scoping (per-namespace isolation of user-supplied instances): a property of the same configuration surface; bundled rather than split.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfd2a0f76a0d748","agent_id":"ac4f00ce08696bdb4","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"a40534c6-bd37-4eed-b1a8-3c544957a6ae","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:10:23.081Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-954071b2bc0067ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final re-review of RHAISTRAT-8004"}
