r) to an OGX instance so that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows run against it. The documentation is a primary work product of this outcome, not incidental polish — the Staff Engineer Input notes that the playground largely abstracts OGX from users, so the written procedure is where the configuration burden lands. It is a separate docs-authoring epic because code implementation and content authoring are different kinds of work with different review criteria, and it is scheduled docs-last: the guide is finalized and technically reviewed only after the configuration support it describes has landed.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Author the end-to-end setup guide: preparing a PostgreSQL+pgvector instance, creating the credentials Secret, configuring the OGXServer spec with the PostgreSQL connection details, and verifying RAG works.\n49\t- Cover the disconnected-install path, where the user's PostgreSQL must be reachable from the cluster.\n50\t- Document the credentials Secret handling and the connection-details format, consistent with the secret-reference (never inline) convention the configuration support enforces.\n51\t- Cross-link the playground's no-vector-store indication to the documented configuration path so the guidance is discoverable from the UI.\n52\t\n53\tOut of scope: the configuration support itself (OGXServer spec fields, credentials Secret wiring, playground indication — delivered by the bring-your-own implementation epic of this branch); the OGX-side remote pgvector provider enablement; benchmarking and resource sizing; Auto Rag compatibility (RHAISTRAT-7824).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The documented setup procedure is complete and has been validated on a clean environment, including the credentials Secret handling and connection details format, and including the disconnected-install path.\n58\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation as built (the configuration support actually delivered, not as planned), and the review is recorded.\n59\t- The documented configuration path remains the migration target for users outgrowing any future default store (consistent with the migration path off the default vector database).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-1 (P0, fallback form)** — in this branch the out-of-the-box default is explicitly not delivered; the documented setup procedure is the user-facing deliverable through which the bring-your-own requirement is met to the extent the Staff Engineer Input directs for this outcome.\n64\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — the clean-environment walk-through of the documented procedure is the end-to-end validation that playground RAG workflows function with the user-provided vector store with no loss of current capability.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfd2a0f76a0d748","agent_id":"ac4f00ce08696bdb4","session_id":"6c664dc7-c756-4423-855a-2ea0889c4084","uuid":"5ea5e47f-0dab-4d21-821e-af6916700492","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:10:24.094Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8aa412f73284eabc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final re-review of RHAISTRAT-8004"}
